https://esolangs.org/wiki/Brainfuck_speed_test

Found on ESOLang.org and is quite fun to try and optimised the bf interepreter
to get it to be faster than other implementations.  I have found that when my
implementation https://omareq.github.io/bf-interpreter/ is run on google 
chrome on an i5 processor it will reach approimately a 20ms runtime.  This is of 
course depending on what other things the js engine is deciding to do at the 
same time.  This is actually comparable to the https://github.com/sreekotay/bffsree
implementation written in c which achieved approximately a 50ms runtime. 
]